  "validation_command": "python scripts/tools/validate_historical_hierarchy.py",
  "rules": [
    "Layer 8 (assets/provinces.json) is the only source of territorial geometry for every higher hierarchy level.",
    "Region may contain only explicit stable province_ids from layer 8; no centroid, bbox, nearest-neighbour, coordinate or shape guessing is allowed.",
    "Superregion may contain only Regions; Macroregion only Superregions; Major Region only Macroregions.",
    "No hierarchy object may carry its own polygon/rings/bbox/coordinates geometry.",
    "A layer-8 province may belong to one Region only, and every child may have one parent only at each higher tier.",
    "A historical Region may not silently mix provinces from different countries.",
    "If a layer-8 province is too coarse or crosses a finer historical boundary, use Province = Region temporarily instead of forcing a historically false union.",
    "Every authored Region must record an internet source and a historical_basis; unverified world areas remain absent instead of being guessed.",
    "Cross-country higher groupings are allowed only when they are an explicit, historically/geographically justified project grouping (for example Iberia or the approved Atlantic archipelagos grouping)."
  ],
